>  <GRAPH_SOURCE>
Single-point calculation on the original coordinates and ligand-by-ligand Lewis review

>  <SOURCE_REFERENCES>
["https://doi.org/10.1002/wcms.1606","https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jctc.8b01176","https://doi.org/10.1039/c3dt52598h","https://github.com/jensengroup/xyz2mol_tm/blob/db2734b084045ef895528c7a3d5040d38da23983/SMILES_csvs/csd_smiles.csv","https://github.com/jensengroup/xyz2mol_tm/blob/db2734b084045ef895528c7a3d5040d38da23983/SMILES_csvs/tmqmg_smiles.csv","https://github.com/uiocompcat/tmQMg/tree/e1dc9887b8f20a217a1db6ca972d726bcbaab45b","https://www.crystallography.net/cod/7024019.cif"]

>  <SELECTION_REASON>
Single-point calculation on the original coordinates and ligand-by-ligand Lewis review. The input contains two terminal CO groups, two ortho-phenylene skeletons and four three-coordinate R₃Si centres. The weak Si···C(CO) contacts are approximately 2.24 Å long, Both electronic-structure methods give bond orders of about 0.3, Treat these as secondary contacts. For the H32 model use the ionic limit of four formal R₃Si⁻ groups and Fe(+4); The reported Si–H description and alternative electronic assignments are retained separately. Localized 12 aromatic-ring bonds using WBOs and original bond lengths. Use the supplied Lewis representation for scoring; Independent evidence for the complete graph is limited.

>  <UPSTREAM_COMPARISON>
Not equivalent

>  <SPIN_REVIEW>
Not independently verified

